# Electroacoustic Performance of Direct-Input Hearing Aids with FM Amplification Systems.

**Authors:** Thibodeau, Linda M.

## Abstract
The electroacoustic performance of 18 direct-input and two inductive-coupling hearing aids was compared when operating with two different frequency modulation (FM) systems. The most significant differences occurred in full-on gain, equivalent-input noise, and frequency response, as opposed to high frequency average saturation sound pressure level or harmonic distortion measurements. (JDD)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ405263

